ction" :answer-field/id #uuid "483a4754-6d02-545b-9ae5-33ad91247c59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79566/selection/fc3219213283e6b7d59e54c9a1eb85d260f550bd227aeef3019879b71977a775" :answer-field/choices ["q-79566/selection/9507af772221d964a38374c4ff249225a8463d5426dde3edc12a44e5dab53462" "q-79566/selection/fc3219213283e6b7d59e54c9a1eb85d260f550bd227aeef3019879b71977a775" "q-79566/selection/9a5a96854cffc7093eb431fe1fcfc48d2a44064ba011be30c6bc76305ef98875" "q-79566/selection/3c837a3e91439d09f6ffc719de9cd105d9c0bf0a7367b2160fe6e84a73614a45" "q-79566/selection/aae33d916e2bcca6b2f9bcb770f5b0cc149c16980014d333cd3b15bbb2421a1d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79566" :question/id #uuid "25e3b8dc-e3e5-5325-8d9f-6db3f8383640" :question/math-academy-id "q-79566" :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{2}(x+2)^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{2}(x+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int (x+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(x+2)^{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-1,0,1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/2ef13d3c7516974afcb94986ee9198b61d263f0ef53c344c02a5a8eb849e2c38.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79566/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23789a74-f1e3-5e26-8678-21f84a11a12b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79566"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119075/selection/01dc157c6856818a6234191013d0423475ad97e0cf9474b33a1dbf6ca66d3e17" :answer/id #uuid "82ac090d-6697-5663-8182-c7a3855f22e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2{x}^{2}-2{e}^{-2x}+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119075/selection/72cffe7e192828f7f48cfdd6d756ae7f345a7d2dd13e79a8b55817279ea2daf0" :answer/id #uuid "91cc5a24-4a6d-57ad-b0a1-131a6d449488" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119075/selection/7b24ddf8b7855f05374d932d7177889c732aba14d72aa536e604f0f81dc206ec" :answer/id #uuid "20d08c01-ca11-5f10-886e-0e0b05769ca7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119075/selection/42893716bcc6ece0d0db1f4849c7dcbd2a6dbed01d02c2c47f464e616ed0b53f" :answer/id #uuid "673c97ea-db18-5cf4-8ac2-16a511a9cff9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=8{x}^{2}+2{e}^{-2x}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119075/selection/2c713aa5652ec6eef12aee525a8bf31a61221c2c759f292401d8f17b3cd6da93" :answer/id #uuid "ce92a6ae-f1fb-5e9a-81d8-2f58ee08fdc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119075/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "91e56ac5-ece3-5602-baa2-12a9baa3ced5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-119075/selection/7b24ddf8b7855f05374d932d7177889c732aba14d72aa536e604f0f81dc206ec" :answer-field/choices ["q-119075/selection/01dc157c6856818a6234191013d0423475ad97e0cf9474b33a1dbf6ca66d3e17" "q-119075/selection/72cffe7e192828f7f48cfdd6d756ae7f345a7d2dd13e79a8b55817279ea2daf0" "q-119075/selection/7b24ddf8b7855f05374d932d7177889c732aba14d72aa536e604f0f81dc206ec" "q-119075/selection/42893716bcc6ece0d0db1f4849c7dcbd2a6dbed01d02c2c47f464e616ed0b53f" "q-119075/selection/2c713aa5652ec6eef12aee525a8bf31a61221c2c759f292401d8f17b3cd6da93"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119075" :question/id #uuid "628de31a-0131-5bc3-8d96-da42a627646b" :question/math-academy-id "q-119075" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}+{e}^{-2x}=8x$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=8x-{e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (8x-{e}^{-2x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =8\\int x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int {e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})-(-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2})+C \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(0)=1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =4(0)^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2(0)}}{2}+C \\\\ 1 & =0+\\frac{1}{2}+C \\\\ C & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-119075/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4ab07a7-d1ed-5f44-8915-09e7b2418825"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119075"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-50159/selection/74516c61d89c746f391c9c9e006c06494fabfc34cf9f46dde232c493d63f7f11" :answer/id #uuid "40b8c4b3-1135-53f6-ba18-b4f1d1ed8581" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50159/selection/ef13043d2c9c13a920d81f0fbafdf021debc150116b67e0e58994ad141a7627f" :answer/id #uuid "69eeaab9-d686-586d-825f-a8f5217dc0f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}+x-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50159/selection/3edf3b2e69007add3afdb6f1c7ce8eedb740df341f44de878318e14ea21b857e" :answer/id #uuid "a06ecdcf-6765-50a7-8618-93b2d122a043" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x)=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50159/selection/36e455560933feeb5462ef9629094aefb1a557c45eb703fad14ee7fd828323d7" :answer/id #uuid "2d847047-23bf-53d1-a78a-76fd499a9bab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x)=2x-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50159/selection/db53952d30628c6fe1dc02d08c880aa03ca331bdf36a9fdd0ce12d71594d5f7f" :answer/id #uuid "a073ad41-29cd-56f3-942f-cdf8b2e09d59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50159/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "de175db1-df03-514c-b7db-688891b19665" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-50159/selection/74516c61d89c746f391c9c9e006c06494fabfc34cf9f46dde232c493d63f7f11" :answer-field/choices ["q-50159/selection/74516c61d89c746f391c9c9e006c06494fabfc34cf9f46dde232c493d63f7f11" "q-50159/selection/ef13043d2c9c13a920d81f0fbafdf021debc150116b67e0e58994ad141a7627f" "q-50159/selection/3edf3b2e69007add3afdb6f1c7ce8eedb740df341f44de878318e14ea21b857e" "q-50159/selection/36e455560933feeb5462ef9629094aefb1a557c45eb703fad14ee7fd828323d7" "q-50159/selection/db53952d30628c6fe1dc02d08c880aa03ca331bdf36a9fdd0ce12d71594d5f7f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-50159" :question/id #uuid "0441f582-d4ce-5255-9837-f92abb18b7b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-50159" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation below that satisfies the condition $f(0)=-2.$\n\n$$\n(1+2x){f}^{′}(x)-2=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{2}{1+2x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2}{1+2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =\\int \\frac{2}{1+2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=(1+2x).$ Then $\\text{d}u=2\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\int \\frac{2}{1+2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(0)=-2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|+C \\\\ -2 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2\\cdot 0|+C \\\\ -2 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|+C \\\\ C & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-50159/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4ab07a7-d1ed-5f44-8915-09e7b2418825"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-50159"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352075/field-1/7f222a04ebc009a0eec97986c36a6bb2943af618882ad465f78dcc4f1341f48f" :answer/id #uuid "08fb583b-06b4-5e74-b8c7-7ee87b6ec923" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\cos(x)-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352075/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4979caa1-2149-50a8-be09-1cac467c30fc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352075/field-1/7f222a04ebc009a0eec97986c36a6bb2943af618882ad465f78dcc4f1341f48f" :answer-field/choices ["q-352075/field-1/7f222a04ebc009a0eec97986c36a6bb2943af618882ad465f78dcc4f1341f48f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352075" :question/id #uuid "70c980cd-81fa-5291-8d3c-a2e45e768133" :question/math-academy-id "q-352075" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${f}^{′}(x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0$ that satisfies the condition $f(0)=2.$\n\n$f(x)=\\,${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =-3\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $f(x)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(0)=2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+C \\\\ 2 & =3(1)+C \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-352075/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4ab07a7-d1ed-5f44-8915-09e7b2418825"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352075"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-530"] :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\ny = x^2+C.\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/e37771799ef5fadc259e6ea0073042a83e0974b5a2619d1af3e87a7467e6d780.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
